                <pb facs="0367" n="265" sameAs="frus:frus1933v03/pg265"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">793.94 Advisory Committee/33: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Minister in Switzerland (Wilson) to the Secretary
                        of State</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Geneva</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1933-04-01T12:00:00+01:00">April 1,
                        1933—noon</date>.<lb/>[Received April 1—8:20 a.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>160. Your 92, March 31, 6 p.m. I entirely share your views as to the
                    inadvisability of our accepting any responsibility as to a decision which
                    rightly rests with the League of Nations. Nothing was further from my mind than
                    to urge such a course. My telegrams which I have just reviewed were written with
                    the idea of conveying a warning as to how the situation was developing here.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Wilson</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
